**What the helper does**

* It receives the node **as a string** (`JSON.stringify(node)`).
* It receives the desired label (`"loopEnd"`).
* Internally it checks whether the current label matches the supplied one.
  * If it does, it simply returns the original node unchanged.
  * If it doesn’t, it constructs a brand‑new break node with the new label and returns that.

**Why this works**

Because the helper guarantees that the returned node always has the correct label, you can safely swap it into your AST without worrying about accidental side‑effects. If the node was already labeled `"loopEnd"`, the helper will just hand back the same node, so your replacement step won’t alter anything.

